<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Install",
    subtitle: "Install the mounted profile and users-reporting addon into a host application.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Host application setup",
    subtitle: "The installer mounts RecordingStudioUser and creates its initializer when they are not already present.",
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    language: :bash,
    code: <<~CODE
      # Gemfile
      gem "recording_studio_user"

      bundle install
      bin/rails generate recording_studio_user:install
    CODE
  ) %>

  <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-(--surface-content-color)">
    Rerunning the installer is idempotent while the generated mount declaration remains intact. It mounts the engine
    with the <code>recording_studio_users</code> proxy and does not overwrite an existing initializer. When Tailwind
    is detected and its <code>@import "tailwindcss"</code> directive is present, it adds missing RecordingStudioUser
    and FlatPack source directives; otherwise it reports the source configuration to add manually.
  </p>

  <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Default URLs",
    subtitle: "The mounted proxy follows the configured mount and route paths.",
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    language: :text,
    code: <<~CODE
      My profile: /recording_studio_users/profile
      Users admin: /recording_studio_users/admin
    CODE
  ) %>

  <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-(--surface-content-color)">
    The host owns the <code>User</code> model, Devise authentication, admin root, and RecordingStudioAccessible
    grants. Configure routes before they are drawn, then configure RecordingStudioAdmin access and its site-admin
    recording resolver. RecordingStudioUser does not create users, roles, access grants, admin roots, or migrations.
  </p>
</div>
